  "slug": "mitochondrial-resource-16ed",
  "summary": "Recent work applies selection-bias correction, survival pseudo-observations, and replicability testing to association data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is whether association estimates hold up before they are interpreted. The review of ten GWAS selection-bias methods, organized by selection type and data availability, addresses distortion directly, with an R repository. The rhesus macaque study applies restricted-mean survival pseudo-observations to exome variants, linking resilience-associated genes to fibrosis and longevity. The microbiome PheWAS of 12.8M gut microbial SNVs against 244 host phenotypes reports 940 associations and a public summary-statistics catalogue. Uniformly re-analysed exercise omics contrasts are pooled through random-effects meta-analysis. The memVar and SheepGTEx entries are primarily resources rather than bias-correction methods. What is new here is the emphasis on correcting or quantifying bias and testing reproducibility before associations are interpreted.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
